<article class="env-lemma" id="EFDBFA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/EFDBFA">Lemma <span data-tag="EFDBFA">6.5.2.3</span>.</a> Let $p: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a Cartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories, let $\calC '$ be a full subcategory of $\calC $, and suppose that for every $p$-Cartesian morphism $f: C \rightarrow C'$ in $\calC $, if $C' \in \calC '$, then $C \in \calC '$. Let $D$ be an object of $\calD $, and let $f: C \rightarrow C'$ be a morphism in the fiber $\calC _{D} = \calC \times _{\calD } \{ D\} $ which exhibits $C'$ as a $\calC ^{0}_{D}$-localization of $C$ (see Definition <a href="/tag/75502E" data-tag="75502E">5.2.7.6</a>). Then $f$ exhibits $C'$ as a $\calC $-localization of $\calC $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Proposition <a href="/tag/B38B7D" data-tag="B38B7D">2.4.3.3</a>, $p$ induces a Cartesian fibration $\calC _{C/} \rightarrow \calD _{D/}$, which restricts to give a Cartesian fibration $p': \calC '_{C/} \rightarrow \calD _{D/}$. We observe that $f$ is an object of $\calC '_{C/}$ which is an initial object of $(p')^{-1} \{  \id _{D} \} $ (Remark <a href="/tag/6072A8" data-tag="6072A8">5.2.7.7</a>), and that $\id _{D}$ is an initial object of $\calD _{D/}$. Lemma <a href="/tag/70D9EC" data-tag="70D9EC">2.4.4.7</a> implies that $f$ is an initial object of $\calC '_{C/}$, so that $f$ exhibits $C'$ as $\calC '$-localization of $C$ (Remark <a href="/tag/6072A8" data-tag="6072A8">5.2.7.7</a>) as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>